## Common Mistakes to Avoid

1. ❌ **Missing file header comments** - Every file needs them!
2. ❌ **No user ownership filter** - Security vulnerability
3. ❌ **Using `any` type** - Defeats TypeScript's purpose
4. ❌ **Forgetting to validate inputs** - Use assert() consistently
5. ❌ **Not writing tests** - Tests are mandatory
6. ❌ **Committing type errors** - Run `npm run type-check` first
7. ❌ **Missing TODO comments** - Document future work
8. ❌ **Hardcoded values** - Use constants and environment variables

